values ('e7f8a9b0-1c2d-4e84-9f34-4b5c6d7e8f44', 'teaching-english-language-learners-tesol-methods', 'Teaching English Language Learners / TESOL Methods', 'This course prepares MEd students to design, teach, assess, and reflect on instruction for English language learners and multilingual students. Students study second language acquisition, WIDA standards, SIOP, sheltered instruction, translanguaging, academic language, multilingual literacy, culturally sustaining pedagogy, assessment equity, family engagement, and program/legal contexts. The course emphasizes asset-based instruction that integrates language development with meaningful content learning.');

